nsight-perf provides an imported INTERFACE target:

    find_package(unofficial-nsight-perf CONFIG REQUIRED)
    target_link_libraries(main PRIVATE unofficial::nsight-perf::nsight-perf)

There is no import library. The SDK ships a shim header
(windows-desktop-x64/nvperf_grfx_host_impl.h) that loads nvperf_grfx_host.dll with
LoadLibrary/GetProcAddress, so exactly one translation unit includes that header and
the DLL is found next to the executable at run time.

The SDK itself is not redistributed by this port. Set the NSIGHT_PERF_SDK environment
variable to the extracted SDK root before running vcpkg; the port locates nvperf_host.h,
the NvPerfUtility headers and nvperf_grfx_host.dll anywhere beneath it, so the package
layout does not matter. The variable must also be listed in VCPKG_ENV_PASSTHROUGH in the
triplet, or the port cannot see it. With the variable unset the port installs an empty
stub and the engine builds without hardware counter support.

Sampling counters also needs run-time permission: NVIDIA Control Panel >
Developer > Manage GPU Performance Counters > allow all users, or an elevated process.
Otherwise the driver returns ERR_NVGPUCTRPERM.
